From 32e2443607038a9472f6f017cf5b6154649f7b1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AItelier wechat-bridge fork <noreply@aitelier.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:03:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Carry every incoming message type out of the addon

The addon decided which messages exist: incoming_text dropped anything whose type
was not 1 before TypeScript could look at it, so images (3), voice (34), video
(43), stickers (47), app messages and quoted replies (49/57) and system notices
(10000) never left native code.

The addon is a protocol client, not a policy. It now drops outgoing only and
reports WeChat's own message type with the raw content/inline_data bytes (base64),
so the consumer can see what arrived. Which arriving types may enter a
conversation stays the consumer's decision: the bridge admits text only, and system
notices and app messages stay out of conversations until a rule says otherwise.

Text is unchanged: type 1 keeps the same JSON shape, the sender-in-content group
split, and a group message without a valid sender is still skipped, never credited
to the group.

The Puppet maps the payload: text stays Text, image/voice/video/sticker map to
their Wechaty types, and every type this puppet does not model - a system notice
included - is Unknown, never Text, so WeChat's own announcement cannot read as a
member speaking.
